and that's that yesterday three crew
members were killed and four others

3
00:00:07,531 --> 00:00:11,493
injured when a Houthi ballistic missile
struck the merchant vessel True Confidence,

4
00:00:11,773 --> 00:00:16,476
a Barbados-flagged, Liberian-owned bulk carrier. The
ship has since been abandoned,

5
00:00:16,556 --> 00:00:20,598
and Operation Prosperity Guardian warships
are on scene assessing the situation.

6
00:00:20,858 --> 00:00:22,840
The casualties are the first among
commercial

7
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,902
ship mariners in the months of Houthi
attacks

8
00:00:25,042 --> 00:00:29,326
following the Israel-Hamas war that broke
out on October 7th. Since that time,

9
00:00:29,406 --> 00:00:30,667
the Houthis have launched more than

10
00:00:31,087 --> 00:00:34,030
45 missile and drone attacks against
commercial and U.S.

11
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:36,512
coalition naval vessels operating in the
Red Sea.

12
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:40,556
Most of those attacks were effectively
countered by U.S. or coalition destroyers

13
00:00:40,856 --> 00:00:44,579
or carrier-based fighters or landed
harmlessly in the water. To date,

14
00:00:44,659 --> 00:00:47,560
no military vessels have been hit by
Houthi UAVs or missiles.

15
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:51,101
One did get close enough to the USS
Gravely to force the destroyer to

16
00:00:51,201 --> 00:00:54,602
use its close-in weapon system. But more
than a dozen commercial ships,

17
00:00:54,882 --> 00:00:58,343
including several US-owned vessels, have
been hit since October.

18
00:00:58,623 --> 00:01:00,824
In spite of the robust naval presence in
the region,

19
00:01:01,004 --> 00:01:02,924
anchored by the aircraft carrier
Eisenhower

20
00:01:03,144 --> 00:01:05,585
and four guided missile destroyers in the
strike group,

21
00:01:05,645 --> 00:01:07,845
along with warships from several partner
nations,

22
00:01:07,885 --> 00:01:09,866
including the UK, France, and India,

23
00:01:10,086 --> 00:01:13,147
the Houthi threat to traffic in the Red
Sea and Gulf of Aden remains.

24
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:15,328
Even four waves of airstrikes by

25
00:01:15,508 --> 00:01:19,811
UK and US jets against targets around the
capital of Sana'a haven't stopped them.

26
00:01:20,091 --> 00:01:23,353
And the Pentagon still does not have a
quote unquote denominator

27
00:01:23,554 --> 00:01:26,716
that gives an assessment of the percentage
of Houthi equipment the coalition has

28
00:01:26,876 --> 00:01:28,597
actually destroyed with the airstrikes.

29
00:01:28,997 --> 00:01:32,320
Deputy Pentagon Press Secretary Sabrina
Singh said last week,

30
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:36,984
we know that the Houthis maintain a large
arsenal. They are very capable.

31
00:01:37,404 --> 00:01:38,866
They have sophisticated weapons,

32
00:01:38,886 --> 00:01:41,148
and that's because they continue to get
them from Iran.

33
00:01:41,628 --> 00:01:44,871
Another senior defense official told the
Pentagon Press Corps that, quote,

34
00:01:45,071 --> 00:01:46,472
they continue to surprise us.

35
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:49,695
We just don't have a good idea of what
they still have, end quote.

36
00:01:50,372 --> 00:01:51,813
I learned a lot at the Naval Academy,

37
